codeExercise.solution:
const delay = (ms, value) => new Promise(resolve => setTimeout(() => resolve(value), ms));

function promiseAll(values) {
  return new Promise((resolve, reject) => {
    const items = Array.from(values);
    const results = new Array(items.length);
    let remaining = items.length;
    if (remaining === 0) { resolve(results); return; }
    items.forEach((value, index) => {
      Promise.resolve(value).then(result => {
        results[index] = result;
        remaining -= 1;
        if (remaining === 0) resolve(results);
      }, reject);
    });
  });
}

codeExercise.solutionNote:
**The plausible wrong answer:**

```js
async function promiseAll(values) {
  const results = [];
  for (const value of values) results.push(await value); // awaits one at a time
  return results;
}
```

This version returns the right values in the happy path, but it only sees a rejection once the loop reaches it, and it never settles if an earlier input hangs. It reveals **`js-execution-model.m2`**: the learner is treating `await` as if it "pauses everything," so waiting on each input in turn seems equivalent to waiting on all of them. In reality the other promises keep settling while the loop waits, and their rejections go unobserved.

codeExercise.testSource:
describe('promiseAll', () => {
  it('keeps input order even when results arrive out of order', async () => {
    await expect(promiseAll([delay(30, 'soup'), 'bread', Promise.resolve('tea')])).resolves.toEqual(['soup', 'bread', 'tea']);
  });
  it('resolves an empty input to an empty array', async () => {
    await expect(promiseAll([])).resolves.toEqual([]);
  });
  it('rejects with the first rejection reason', async () => {
    await expect(promiseAll([delay(10, 'soup'), Promise.reject(new Error('burnt'))])).rejects.toThrow('burnt');
  });
  it('rejects without waiting for a pending input that never settles', async () => {
    const never = new Promise(() => {});
    const outcome = await Promise.race([
      promiseAll([never, Promise.reject(new Error('burnt'))]).catch(() => 'rejected'),
      delay(100, 'still pending'),
    ]);
    expect(outcome).toBe('rejected');
  });
});

